  "update_count": 69,
  "description_snippet": "### Summary\r\n\r\nA specific JavaScript code can trigger a memory corruption in V8 7.3.492.17 which could potentially be abused for remote code execution. In order to trigger this vulnerability in the context of a browser, such as Google Chrome, the victim would need to visit a malicious web page."
